{
  "dom_id": "question-114542",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267484/assets/0914f8235416209716e6df9a22df72439a7c33de9cca40b8326bd749b0188ac4.png)\n\nWhich of the following combinations of transformations map the polygon $ABCDEF$ to a congruent polygon?\n\nI. A reflection in the axis $\\overset{⟷}{BC},$ followed by a vertical stretch of scale factor $2.$\n\nII. A  translation of $1$ unit to the left and $1$ unit down, followed by a rotation of ${53}^{∘}$ counterclockwise about the point $A.$\n\nIII. A dilation of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ with the center of dilation $A,$ followed by a reflection in the line $\\overset{⟷}{AD}.$",
